    <briefdescription>
<para>Logical OR comparator struct template. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Derived from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op" kindref="compound">binary_op</ref></computeroutput>, this struct combines two sub-expressions with a logical OR operation. It enables composition of complex assertions by combining multiple conditions into a single logical whole, with reporting that shows the combined result and individual operand outcomes.</para>
<para>The sub-expressions are not copied: the temporaries are moved into the comparator, and the named ones are referred to (see <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a85cd019d0861a4b6d62c3424f4a8931d" kindref="member">stored_operand_t</ref></computeroutput>).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the stored left-hand sub-expression, either its type, or a <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> reference to it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the stored right-hand sub-expression, either its type, or a <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> reference to it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
